;; The tools an AI agent may call on a plant, checked before they ship.
;;
;; An agent reaches equipment only through the gateway component's exported
;; tools, and the gateway reaches equipment only through what it imports.
;; Its imports are in its binary, so "can the agent write a register?" is
;; answered by reading the artifact, not by trusting a configuration file.
;;
;; The tree below is what makes that a Silt question. Its vocabulary is every
;; interface under br2-external/wit — this pack's own (silt:modbus,
;; silt:gateway) and WASI 0.2.6, vendored so that policy can name the WASI
;; interfaces too. An import outside that vocabulary is a finding: a policy
;; cannot forbid what it cannot name, so the check fails closed.

(pack agent-gateway
  (version "0.1.0")
  (doc "An agent gateway whose reach is checked from its binary")

  (requires
    (buildroot "2025.02.16"))

  (external "br2-external")

  (provides
    (feature agent-gateway)
    (feature agent-read-only)))
